          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_automorphisms_of_the_exceptional_jordan_algebra As automorphisms of the exceptional Jordan algebra
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            = succeed "-preserving" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            of the vector space underlying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+Albert+algebra"} octonionic Albert algebra
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mn 6
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 26
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {E}_{6(-26)}
            = succeed "))." do
              %a{:href => "#ManogueDray09"} Manogue-Dray 09
          %p
            This may be written as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(3,\mathbb{O})
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DrayManogue09a"} Dray-Manogue 09a (16)
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MapOfE6.png", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from (
              %a{:href => "#DrayManogue09a"}> Dray-Manogue 09a, p. 12
              )
          %h3#outer_automorphism Outer automorphism
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_6
            has 2-fold symmetry, corresponding to a nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/outer+automorphism"} outer automorphism
            of order 2.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_6
            acts on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+projective+plane"} octonionic projective plane
            and its outer automorphism gives rise to a projective duality in its geometry.
